# What each bundle version actually contained.
#
# `VERSION` on its own is a claim, and the repository had no way to check it: a
# listed file could change while the number stayed put, leaving two materially
# different bundles both recording the same version. That happened twice in one
# train -- the keyring changed `docker-compose.yml` and the runtime preflight,
# and the rotation verb changed the deploy wrapper -- and no test noticed
# either time.
#
# One line per version: `<version> <sha256>`, where the digest covers the
# inventory plus the content of every file it lists. `ops/tests/host-bundle.sh`
# recomputes the digest for the current `VERSION` and fails if it disagrees, so
# changing a bundle file forces a decision here instead of allowing silence.
# Appending a line is the normal outcome; editing one is rewriting the recorded
# identity of a bundle that may already be installed on a host.
#
# The ledger starts at 5 because earlier bundles predate it and their contents
# cannot be recovered from this tree.
